  <properties>
    <!--
      The build JDK stays 25 (see requireJavaVersion below); only the bytecode
      target drops. Android's D8 refuses class files above major version 65, so
      every module the app links against must be compiled at release 21 or
      lower — and the app's compile closure is mw-core, mw-audio, mw-dsp,
      mw-transcribe, mw-arrange and mw-notation, most of the reactor. (mw-ml was
      in that closure too until #247 took mw-transcribe's unused edge to it out.)

      A survey of those modules found no post-21 language feature and no post-21
      API in main or test sources: the whole reactor compiles clean at 21, so
      lowering it here rather than overriding it in six module poms costs
      nothing and leaves one number to read instead of several to keep in step.
      The enforcer rule below stops it drifting back up, and
      AndroidBytecodeTargetTest checks the class files themselves, which is what
      D8 actually reads.
    -->
    <maven.compiler.release>21</maven.compiler.release>
    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
    <project.reporting.outputEncoding>UTF-8</project.reporting.outputEncoding>

    <!--
      Dependency versions. Every coordinate below was verified present on
      Maven Central. Licensing policy: Apache/MIT/BSD preferred, LGPL permitted
      as an unmodified library dependency, GPL/AGPL banned outright.
      See CONTRIBUTING.md for the rationale.
    -->
